Keeps the LMS positions of libsais_main_8u's first pass over T for after
the recursion, where the free space allows, instead of finding them
again.

After the recursion has sorted the reduced string, libsais_main_8u maps
its suffix array back to positions in T through the list of LMS
positions, which it rebuilds with a second classification pass over T
(libsais_gather_lms_suffixes_8u_omp, which 2.12.0 vectorises with SSE2
or AVX2 and NEON; without them, one loop over the block's two halves
interleaved). Here the list from the first pass is copied into the last
m ints of the free space, and the top level and the recursion work in
the fs - m ints below it. That is done only where fs >= m, which puts
the copy beyond SA[0..n), and fs + n >= 4m, which leaves the recursion
fs + n - 3m >= m ints of free space, at least its length: a level's free
space less its length never decreases down the recursion and a level's
alphabet is smaller than its length, so the recursion still never
allocates. Elsewhere the positions are found again as before. The suffix
array is the same either way. 2.12.0's naming of nonunique LMS
substrings before the recursion works inside SA[0..n) and does not reach
the copy.

Only libsais_main_8u changes, and every entry that reaches it (libsais,
libsais_gsa, libsais_bwt, libsais_bwt_aux, libsais_bwt_cyclic and their
_ctx forms) takes the same path. The recursion's levels still find their
own positions again: in most of its bucket layouts that pass also
recounts the buckets, which the deeper levels overwrite, so keeping the
positions there saves less.

At level 9 the condition holds for every block of a 16 KiB stream and
for the 900 kB blocks of inputs with at most 3/8 LMS positions (XA:Z,
quality strings, ten of the twelve Silesia files), not for those of MC:Z
(0.40) nor for many of Silesia's mr and x-ray (0.48-0.49).

Measured with libsais 2.12.0 on the M4 Max with Apple clang 21, the sort
stage alone (bzng_sort_block on every level-9 block of the corpora, 3
clean rounds interleaved with an identical build as control), the series
with this patch against the same series without it, 16 KiB / 64 KiB /
whole-file streams: XA:Z 1.02 / 1.03 / 1.02, quality strings 1.00 / 1.03
/ 1.01, MC:Z 1.01 / 1.01 / even (its full blocks do not keep the list),
Silesia 1.01; XA:Z in 64 KiB and whole-file streams, quality strings in
64 KiB streams and Silesia faster in every round, the rest inside the
control's noise. On 1a696e6 the same patch gained 1.04-1.06 end to end;
2.12.0's second pass over T is faster, which leaves less to save.

--- a/libsais.c
+++ b/libsais.c
@@ -1,3 +1,11 @@
+/*
+ * Altered for bz2-ng: this is libsais.c of libsais 2.12.0 (commit 2f44d93)
+ * with the following patches from bz2-ng's c/third_party/libsais/patches
+ * applied.
+ *
+ * 0001-keep-lms-positions.patch
+ */
+
 /*--
 
 This file is a part of libsais, a library for linear time suffix array,
@@ -9580,6 +9588,17 @@
         sa_sint_t middle_m            = n >= 65536 ? libsais_count_middle_lms_suffixes(SA, n, m) : 0;
         sa_sint_t middle_lms_suffix   = middle_m > 0 ? SA[n - middle_m] : 0;
 
+        /*
+         * Where the rest of the free space still lets the recursion sort
+         * without allocating, the LMS positions are kept in its last m ints
+         * for after the recursion instead of being found again by a second
+         * pass over T: fs >= m puts the copy beyond SA[0..n), and
+         * fs + n >= 4m leaves the recursion fs + n - 3m >= m ints of free
+         * space, at least its length.
+         */
+        sa_sint_t keep_lms_suffixes = fs >= m && (fs + n) / 4 >= m;
+        if (keep_lms_suffixes) { fs -= m; memcpy(&SA[n + fs], &SA[n - m], (size_t)m * sizeof(sa_sint_t)); }
+
         if (threads > 1 && n >= 65536) { memset(SA, 0, ((size_t)n - (size_t)m) * sizeof(sa_sint_t)); }
         libsais_radix_sort_lms_suffixes_8u_omp(T, SA, n, m, flags, buckets, lms_threads, thread_state);
         if (threads > 1 && n >= 65536) { memset(&SA[(fast_sint_t)n - (fast_sint_t)m], 0, (size_t)m * sizeof(sa_sint_t)); }
@@ -9595,8 +9614,15 @@
                 return -2;
             }
 
-            libsais_gather_lms_suffixes_8u_omp(T, SA, n, middle_lms_suffix, middle_m, lms_threads, thread_state);
-            libsais_reconstruct_lms_suffixes_omp(SA, n, m, threads);
+            if (keep_lms_suffixes)
+            {
+                libsais_reconstruct_lms_suffixes_omp(SA, n + fs + m, m, threads);
+            }
+            else
+            {
+                libsais_gather_lms_suffixes_8u_omp(T, SA, n, middle_lms_suffix, middle_m, lms_threads, thread_state);
+                libsais_reconstruct_lms_suffixes_omp(SA, n, m, threads);
+            }
         }
 
         libsais_place_lms_suffixes_interval_8u(SA, n, m, flags, buckets);
